          "from": "/k/ adjacent to front vowels",
          "to": "kedi /ceˈdi/ 'cat'",
          "note": "In native words /k, ɡ/ are realized as [c, ɟ] next to the front vowels /e, i, œ, y/; in loanwords the palatal is contrastive (kar 'snow' vs kâr [car] 'profit')."
        }
      ]
    },
